ode Hosts India got a pair of golds in the 1500s from Ajay Kumar (3:45) and P U Chitra (4:17).\nAsian Champs Day 1: Iran’s Ethsan Hadadi Highlights By Winning His Fifth Asian Discus Title Super hot conditions (90+ degrees) lead to super slow distance races as the men’s 5000 was won in 14:54 (slowest ever winning time) and the women’s 15:57.\nCaster Semenya On New Testosterone Study: “I Don’t Have Time For Idiots” The current situation with hyperandrogenic athletes isn’t Semenya’s fault, but the truth is there are a lot of very intelligent “non-idiots” who don’t think she should be competing against women without hormone treatment.\nDrew Hunter Wins 3000 In 8:14 As Americans Clean Up At Donegal, Ireland Meet USA also got wins from Kaela Edwards (2:03 – 800), Mel Lawrence (9:36 – steeple) and Robert Domanic (3:59 – mile).\nJo Pavey Ends Bid To Earn Spot On GB’s 2017 World Team Due To Heel Injury Sprinter Adam Gemili might be out of a Worlds spot as well as he pulled out of the Anniversary Games with an injury and he’s relying on committee selection for a spot.\nChristian Coleman Will Only Run The 100 At Worlds With 48-races this year, his coach thought it’d be best to skip the 200.\nRecommended Read: 14-Years Ago Perdita Felicien Became Canada’s First Female World Champion, Winning An Upset 100H Gold Over Jamaica’s Brigitte Foster-Hylton Felicien talks about her 2003 gold, her career and going on to become a sports journalist for the Canadian Broadcasting Corporation after retiring.\nRecommended Read #2: US High Jumper Jamie Nieto Trying To Defy The Doctors To Be Ready To Walk For His July Wedding Nieto suffered a spinal cord injury when doing a backflip in 2016. Doctors weren’t sure if he’d ever walk at all, but now he’s up to 130-steps without a can or walker which should about get him from the altar t","tokens":["–"," C","aster"," Sem","en","ya"," responding"," when"," asked"," for"," her"," views"," on"," the"," recent"," I","AA","F"," and"," W","ADA"," funded"," 